/-!
# Coordinate rings and function fields of incidence components

For tuples `x`, `y`, `z` in an algebraically closed field `Ω` over `k`, with `x` and `z` finite and
algebraic over the field generated by `y`, every irreducible component `Z` of the spectrum of the
incidence ring `k[X, Y, Z] ⧸ (I(x, y) + I(y, z))` with dense image in `Spec (k[Y] ⧸ I(y))` is the
locus of a joint tuple `(x', y, z')` whose pairs have the loci of `(x, y)` and `(y, z)`
(`locusIncidence_dominatingComponents_eq_jointLoci`). Its coordinate ring is the ring generated by
the joint tuple, and its function field is the compositum `k(x', y) ⊔ k(y, z')` inside `Ω`. Both
identifications send the class of a polynomial to its value at the joint tuple
(`exists_locusIncidence_component_algEquiv`).

This is the function-field description of composition in blueprint §8.1: the function field of a
component of `C ×_W D` is the compositum of the two function fields over `k(W)`. The function
field of the endpoint image of a component is the subfield generated by `(x', z')`, which can be
smaller.

This module is part of the formalization of the Evans–Hrushovski–Gismatullin
reconstruction theorem; the source of truth is `sources/blueprint.tex`.

**Status:** proved (#5, C2 support).
-/


